{"requirements":[{"id":"ipv4_icmp_redirects","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The runtime value changed from 1 to 0 for all, default, enp1s0, and lo. The root-owned sysctl configuration persisted across a confirmed reboot, and every observed scope remained 0 afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84f082675190421c","cmd-8a693c4e64064851","cmd-90b7bc48cc654637","cmd-db64b22698e54080","cmd-b4461b9e61554651"]},{"id":"ipv4_source_routing","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 source-routed packets on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All observed scopes reported accept_source_route=0 before and after the reboot, and the persistent configuration explicitly enforces 0 for aggregate, default/future, and current interfaces.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84f082675190421c","cmd-90b7bc48cc654637","cmd-db64b22698e54080","cmd-b4461b9e61554651"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the hardening file and applying the sysctl stack were directly necessary, while the scheduled reboot served both persistence validation and the mandatory restart protocol. The transient reboot unit was consumed by the reboot. Final observations show no failed services, new exposure, package damage, or unrelated residue; socket and temporary-file differences are normal process-ID and systemd-private-directory changes following reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fef3c039138a43cb","cmd-8a693c4e64064851","cmd-db64b22698e54080","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both required IPv4 acceptance controls are disabled and persist across reboot. The node-restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, connection interruption, a different post-restart identity independently corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered system, networking, configuration, and service state were all captured.","limitations":[]}
